1
00:00:07,030 --> 00:00:08,390
"♪Don't stay trapped inside your room♪

2
00:00:08,390 --> 00:00:09,790
♪Outside the window,
the rain has cleared♪

3
00:00:09,790 --> 00:00:11,070
♪Set reality aside♪

4
00:00:11,070 --> 00:00:12,390
♪Follow your heart♪

5
00:00:12,390 --> 00:00:13,750
♪What you've been longing
for is right ahead♪

6
00:00:13,750 --> 00:00:15,230
♪Don't act like you didn't see it♪

7
00:00:15,230 --> 00:00:18,110
♪Just be a little braver♪

8
00:00:18,110 --> 00:00:20,870
♪Come closer, come closer♪

9
00:00:20,870 --> 00:00:23,950
♪There's a little spark
shining in your eyes♪

10
00:00:24,230 --> 00:00:26,070
♪That's the signal
of a heart coming alive♪

11
00:00:28,310 --> 00:00:29,790
♪That's the signal
of a heart coming alive♪"

12
00:00:29,940 --> 00:00:33,820
=Heart Signal (China Version) S9=
(Bonus Edition)

13
00:00:38,900 --> 00:00:41,460
(Yu Yang returns to Signal House)
Hello.

14
00:00:42,280 --> 00:00:43,880
Hi, Yu Yang.

15
00:00:43,880 --> 00:00:44,440
Hello.

16
00:00:44,720 --> 00:00:45,960
Happy Children's Day!

17
00:00:45,960 --> 00:00:47,600
Happy Children's Day, Yu Yang!

18
00:00:47,600 --> 00:00:49,080
Happy Children's Day!

19
00:00:49,080 --> 00:00:50,240
Yu Yang, did you bring any food?

20
00:00:50,520 --> 00:00:51,440
I did.

21
00:00:51,760 --> 00:00:53,480
We all brought a ton of food.

22
00:00:55,360 --> 00:00:56,280
I really did.

23
00:00:57,200 --> 00:00:58,400
What did you bring?

24
00:00:58,400 --> 00:01:01,880
I just brought some stuff
we can eat right away.

25
00:01:01,880 --> 00:01:02,400
Nice.

26
00:01:02,400 --> 00:01:03,360
- Good.
- Yeah.

27
00:01:03,360 --> 00:01:04,600
All right, let's plate everything.

28
00:01:04,600 --> 00:01:05,800
It's like New Year's today.

29
00:01:05,800 --> 00:01:06,320
Okay.

30
00:01:07,920 --> 00:01:09,080
Let's get this out carefully.

31
00:01:09,140 --> 00:01:10,960
(Unpacking the cake)
I think it probably fell apart.

32
00:01:13,840 --> 00:01:15,000
How do we open this?

33
00:01:15,000 --> 00:01:16,160
(Asking)

34
00:01:16,160 --> 00:01:16,880
You open it.

35
00:01:16,880 --> 00:01:17,640
I don't know either.

36
00:01:21,360 --> 00:01:21,840
How do we open it?

37
00:01:21,840 --> 00:01:23,080
We should peel this off, right?

38
00:01:23,080 --> 00:01:23,760
Yeah.

39
00:01:24,200 --> 00:01:25,000
Let's see.

40
00:01:26,360 --> 00:01:27,080
Not bad.

41
00:01:27,080 --> 00:01:28,240
A little messed up.

42
00:01:28,240 --> 00:01:29,560
Let's fix it.

43
00:01:29,560 --> 00:01:30,000
Sure.

44
00:01:30,000 --> 00:01:30,600
This part here.

45
00:01:30,600 --> 00:01:31,400
It's fine.

46
00:01:31,400 --> 00:01:32,680
We just need to move it to the top.

47
00:01:32,680 --> 00:01:34,240
I'll go get a tool.

48
00:01:34,240 --> 00:01:35,320
Yeah.

49
00:01:35,320 --> 00:01:36,360
Do we have a fork?

50
00:01:36,360 --> 00:01:37,200
I don't know.

51
00:01:38,000 --> 00:01:38,800
Maybe we should get two tools.

52
00:01:38,800 --> 00:01:40,360
Oh no, it's falling apart.

53
00:01:40,920 --> 00:01:41,880
It's okay.

54
00:01:44,320 --> 00:01:45,800
How about a spoon?

55
00:01:45,800 --> 00:01:46,720
Sure.

56
00:01:52,440 --> 00:01:53,480
Let's put it on first.

57
00:01:53,480 --> 00:01:54,640
Then we'll spread it out.

58
00:01:56,320 --> 00:01:57,000
Like this.

59
00:01:57,560 --> 00:01:59,160
I'll hold this side up.

60
00:02:01,560 --> 00:02:03,180
Can you tell what shape it is?

61
00:02:03,740 --> 00:02:04,880
(Thinking)

62
00:02:04,880 --> 00:02:06,520
It should be...

63
00:02:09,080 --> 00:02:09,480
A cloud.

64
00:02:14,560 --> 00:02:15,800
I thought it was a little animal.

65
00:02:17,480 --> 00:02:18,800
And then its head fell off.

66
00:02:18,820 --> 00:02:22,580
(Amused)

67
00:02:27,400 --> 00:02:28,800
Slowly, lift it up.

68
00:02:31,520 --> 00:02:32,720
Looks pretty good.

69
00:02:33,880 --> 00:02:34,760
My hands are shaking so much.

70
00:02:35,180 --> 00:02:36,740
(Amused)

71
00:02:36,840 --> 00:02:37,680
Not bad.

72
00:02:37,680 --> 00:02:38,120
Good.

73
00:02:48,240 --> 00:02:48,920
Nice.

74
00:02:56,000 --> 00:02:57,400
This actually looks pretty nice.

75
00:02:58,080 --> 00:02:58,840
Yeah.

76
00:02:59,440 --> 00:03:01,080
You can eat the apple for me.

77
00:03:01,080 --> 00:03:02,840
Okay, I'll eat the apple for you.

78
00:03:02,840 --> 00:03:03,960
There's more apple in here.
You want some?

79
00:03:03,960 --> 00:03:05,100
There's more apple?

80
00:03:05,100 --> 00:03:05,440
Yeah.

81
00:03:05,440 --> 00:03:06,480
Should I scoop it out?

82
00:03:06,680 --> 00:03:07,120
Sure.

83
00:03:10,800 --> 00:03:11,880
This apple should be

84
00:03:11,880 --> 00:03:13,520
a little sweet.

85
00:03:13,520 --> 00:03:14,320
Okay.

86
00:03:16,040 --> 00:03:17,720
I'll eat these two first.

87
00:03:18,720 --> 00:03:19,920
Let me try it.

88
00:03:19,920 --> 00:03:21,280
I'll find a fork.

89
00:03:23,460 --> 00:03:25,940
(Laughing)

90
00:03:33,200 --> 00:03:35,000
Si, do you want to try the cooked apple?

91
00:03:36,000 --> 00:03:37,000
What's this?

92
00:03:37,000 --> 00:03:38,760
It's that cooked apple.

93
00:03:38,840 --> 00:03:39,940
Okay, let's go over there.

94
00:03:39,940 --> 00:03:41,640
- We'll eat it together.
- Okay, sure.

95
00:03:43,480 --> 00:03:45,280
We're already using these bowls.

96
00:03:45,280 --> 00:03:46,200
That's right.

97
00:03:46,520 --> 00:03:47,400
Let me try it first.

98
00:03:50,120 --> 00:03:51,200
Is it good?

99
00:03:52,320 --> 00:03:54,640
It's a sweet, beef-flavored apple.

100
00:03:54,640 --> 00:03:56,160
Beef-flavored?

101
00:03:56,160 --> 00:03:57,960
It was cooked in the pot for a while.

102
00:04:01,500 --> 00:04:03,780
(Liang Renfang comes to the dining room)

103
00:04:04,740 --> 00:04:06,460
(Looking)

104
00:04:06,540 --> 00:04:07,840
(Approaching)

105
00:04:07,840 --> 00:04:08,960
Whose is this?

106
00:04:08,960 --> 00:04:10,200
I brought it.

107
00:04:10,720 --> 00:04:11,760
Healthy food.

108
00:04:12,240 --> 00:04:13,360
I can't eat spicy food.

109
00:04:13,360 --> 00:04:15,080
I prefer light meals.

110
00:04:16,420 --> 00:04:18,300
(Memorizing that)

111
00:04:18,940 --> 00:04:20,580
(Smiling)
Okay.

112
00:04:22,560 --> 00:04:24,120
Let's clean this.

113
00:04:28,450 --> 00:04:29,520
Another one.

114
00:04:29,520 --> 00:04:31,640
Maybe we should clean everything
when we're done.

115
00:04:31,640 --> 00:04:33,960
It's okay.
I'll clean some of this first.

116
00:04:33,960 --> 00:04:35,800
Then we'll have less to do later.

117
00:04:36,480 --> 00:04:37,160
Thanks.

118
00:04:37,400 --> 00:04:38,880
Such a thoughtful woman.

119
00:04:38,880 --> 00:04:39,560
I feel like otherwise,

120
00:04:39,560 --> 00:04:41,600
we'll be exhausted later.

121
00:04:42,980 --> 00:04:43,940
(Glances)

122
00:04:45,000 --> 00:04:46,280
That apple really does

123
00:04:46,280 --> 00:04:48,440
taste like beef.

124
00:04:49,200 --> 00:04:49,840
Really.

125
00:04:49,840 --> 00:04:50,400
Of course.

126
00:04:50,400 --> 00:04:51,440
It was cooked for a while.

127
00:04:51,680 --> 00:04:52,720
It's actually pretty good.

128
00:04:53,080 --> 00:04:54,640
It's pretty unusual.

129
00:04:54,640 --> 00:04:55,800
Usually,

130
00:04:55,800 --> 00:04:56,840
I'd eat the apple first

131
00:04:56,840 --> 00:04:57,400
after cooking it.

132
00:04:57,400 --> 00:04:58,520
You would eat the apple first.

133
00:04:58,520 --> 00:04:58,840
Right.

134
00:04:58,840 --> 00:05:00,560
Otherwise, it gets too sweet

135
00:05:00,720 --> 00:05:01,840
if you leave it too long.

136
00:05:04,920 --> 00:05:06,080
Did you make this?

137
00:05:06,320 --> 00:05:07,040
Yeah.

138
00:05:07,640 --> 00:05:09,040
You seem pretty good at cooking.

139
00:05:09,200 --> 00:05:09,800
Who?

140
00:05:11,880 --> 00:05:12,840
Everyone's good at cooking.

141
00:05:12,840 --> 00:05:14,120
Look at that table.

142
00:05:14,820 --> 00:05:16,920
(Turns to look)
What they made is pretty impressive.

143
00:05:16,920 --> 00:05:18,480
They're all pretty

144
00:05:18,480 --> 00:05:19,040
challenging.

145
00:05:20,080 --> 00:05:20,920
Do you have a tissue?

146
00:05:21,140 --> 00:05:22,860
(Notices)

147
00:05:22,880 --> 00:05:24,760
I'll get you one.

148
00:05:27,320 --> 00:05:27,960
Thank you.

149
00:05:28,360 --> 00:05:29,160
Have a seat.

150
00:05:32,200 --> 00:05:33,000
It's a little spicy.

151
00:05:33,840 --> 00:05:34,440
Never mind then.

152
00:05:34,440 --> 00:05:35,680
I think it is a little spicy.

153
00:05:35,840 --> 00:05:37,160
I ate fried chicken yesterday,

154
00:05:37,160 --> 00:05:37,920
and I broke out.

155
00:05:38,580 --> 00:05:39,780
(Glances)

156
00:05:44,800 --> 00:05:46,000
Didn't see anything.

157
00:05:46,000 --> 00:05:46,560
Nope.

158
00:05:46,820 --> 00:05:48,380
(Smiles)

159
00:05:48,800 --> 00:05:49,840
If I can't see it, it's not there.

160
00:05:49,840 --> 00:05:50,720
Okay.

161
00:05:51,320 --> 00:05:52,160
Fang, I feel like Yu Yang

162
00:05:52,160 --> 00:05:53,440
became so much more relaxed

163
00:05:53,440 --> 00:05:54,560
after spending time with you yesterday.

164
00:05:54,580 --> 00:05:56,020
(Smiles)

165
00:05:56,060 --> 00:05:57,260
(Laughs)

166
00:05:57,260 --> 00:05:58,320
From what I've seen these past few days,

167
00:05:58,320 --> 00:05:59,440
Yu Yang has become a completely

168
00:05:59,440 --> 00:06:00,120
different person.

169
00:06:00,120 --> 00:06:01,760
He was relaxed from head to toe.

170
00:06:02,240 --> 00:06:03,200
Even his brain was relaxed.

171
00:06:08,000 --> 00:06:09,160
Who's your roommate?

172
00:06:09,560 --> 00:06:10,400
My roommate?

173
00:06:10,980 --> 00:06:12,980
(Points)

174
00:06:13,100 --> 00:06:14,720
(Imitates)

175
00:06:14,720 --> 00:06:15,560
What?

176
00:06:16,400 --> 00:06:17,520
What do you mean?

177
00:06:18,600 --> 00:06:19,600
Our secret code.

178
00:06:20,500 --> 00:06:21,820
(Laughs)

179
00:06:23,240 --> 00:06:23,780
Secret code.

180
00:06:23,780 --> 00:06:24,580
That's some serious secret code.

181
00:06:24,740 --> 00:06:26,260
(Laughs)

182
00:06:31,480 --> 00:06:32,640
Let's start washing dishes.

183
00:06:32,880 --> 00:06:33,600
Okay.

184
00:06:33,620 --> 00:06:36,700
(Cleaning up after the meal)

185
00:06:42,520 --> 00:06:43,360
You pick up the chopsticks.

186
00:06:43,360 --> 00:06:44,240
I'll wash the bowls.

187
00:06:44,240 --> 00:06:44,720
Okay.

188
00:06:45,840 --> 00:06:46,920
We're heading out first.

189
00:06:46,920 --> 00:06:47,760
Okay, we'll wash them.

190
00:06:47,760 --> 00:06:48,240
Bye bye.

191
00:06:48,240 --> 00:06:49,240
Bye.

192
00:06:50,200 --> 00:06:51,400
Is it easy to wash them over there?

193
00:06:51,400 --> 00:06:52,280
Why don't you come over here?

194
00:06:54,420 --> 00:06:55,940
(Switches places)

195
00:06:55,960 --> 00:06:57,800
Neither of us is wearing an apron.

196
00:06:57,800 --> 00:06:58,720
Go put one on.

197
00:06:58,720 --> 00:07:00,320
You can wash the dishes.

198
00:07:00,320 --> 00:07:02,160
And I'll wipe the plates.

199
00:07:02,160 --> 00:07:02,800
Okay.

200
00:07:06,520 --> 00:07:08,160
There's some of your flour on this.

201
00:07:08,160 --> 00:07:09,000
Flour.

202
00:07:09,520 --> 00:07:11,080
Flour? That's the one I just wore.

203
00:07:12,080 --> 00:07:13,700
I can't get my hands through it, so...

204
00:07:13,700 --> 00:07:14,360
Then how do you wear it?

205
00:07:14,360 --> 00:07:15,320
Just put it around my neck.

206
00:07:16,640 --> 00:07:17,400
Then let's do it like this.

207
00:07:17,680 --> 00:07:18,440
Let's do it like this.

208
00:07:20,040 --> 00:07:20,880
Like this.

209
00:07:20,880 --> 00:07:22,320
Yeah, I can't get my hands through.

210
00:07:24,020 --> 00:07:24,820
(Laughs)

211
00:07:24,840 --> 00:07:25,880
This is the only way.

212
00:07:27,320 --> 00:07:28,200
That works too.

213
00:07:28,200 --> 00:07:29,920
You seem trapped in there.

214
00:07:30,280 --> 00:07:31,320
Your hands really can't get out?

215
00:07:31,320 --> 00:07:31,680
It's fine.

216
00:07:31,680 --> 00:07:32,400
As long as I can wash.

217
00:07:32,400 --> 00:07:33,440
Then I'll wipe them.

218
00:07:33,440 --> 00:07:34,240
Okay.

219
00:07:38,080 --> 00:07:39,320
Feels like I'm tied up.

220
00:07:39,340 --> 00:07:40,040
(Glances)

221
00:07:40,040 --> 00:07:41,260
I can only wash dishes like this now.

222
00:07:41,260 --> 00:07:42,260
I can't stretch my arms out either.

223
00:07:48,480 --> 00:07:49,840
Come on, you two. Pick two.

224
00:07:50,200 --> 00:07:52,320
You're the first ones to get them.

225
00:07:53,440 --> 00:07:54,480
I'll pick two.

226
00:07:54,480 --> 00:07:55,040
Sure.

227
00:07:56,680 --> 00:07:57,640
Let's go with this one.

228
00:07:57,640 --> 00:07:58,120
Sure.

229
00:07:58,120 --> 00:07:59,000
Take it out.

230
00:07:59,000 --> 00:08:00,400
Is this a tulip?

231
00:08:00,400 --> 00:08:01,080
Yeah.

232
00:08:02,080 --> 00:08:02,800
Okay.

233
00:08:02,800 --> 00:08:04,200
There should be a stem
or something underneath.

234
00:08:04,200 --> 00:08:05,560
I'll get it out for you.

235
00:08:05,560 --> 00:08:06,840
You do it. I'm afraid I'll break it.

236
00:08:06,840 --> 00:08:08,520
It's fine. It won't hurt it.

237
00:08:09,400 --> 00:08:10,000
There.

238
00:08:10,000 --> 00:08:11,720
There should be something
for arranging it.

239
00:08:16,080 --> 00:08:18,400
I literally just ripped it apart.

240
00:08:18,400 --> 00:08:18,880
Beautiful.

241
00:08:18,880 --> 00:08:20,360
Let me see if there's a bigger one.

242
00:08:20,360 --> 00:08:21,880
It's fine. These two are enough.

243
00:08:21,880 --> 00:08:22,600
Let's take this one too.

244
00:08:22,600 --> 00:08:23,800
Okay.

245
00:08:23,800 --> 00:08:25,480
You can put them together.

246
00:08:25,480 --> 00:08:26,880
I'll put them here.

247
00:08:26,880 --> 00:08:27,480
Okay.

248
00:08:27,480 --> 00:08:28,520
We'll take them with us later.

249
00:08:28,520 --> 00:08:29,240
Thanks, Meng.

250
00:08:35,400 --> 00:08:36,200
It's for you.

251
00:08:36,200 --> 00:08:37,280
Thank you.

252
00:08:37,280 --> 00:08:38,120
One for each of you.

253
00:08:38,120 --> 00:08:39,360
Thank you.

254
00:08:39,360 --> 00:08:39,760
This one.

255
00:08:40,520 --> 00:08:42,080
Soak it in water for a while.

256
00:08:42,080 --> 00:08:43,000
Then we can take them

257
00:08:43,000 --> 00:08:45,440
and keep them in our room.

258
00:08:45,960 --> 00:08:47,720
Okay.

259
00:08:49,000 --> 00:08:49,680
Si.

260
00:08:50,800 --> 00:08:51,560
Here's one for you.

261
00:08:51,560 --> 00:08:52,360
Pick one.

262
00:08:52,840 --> 00:08:53,520
Thank you.

263
00:08:54,360 --> 00:08:55,360
It's orange.

264
00:08:55,920 --> 00:08:56,480
So pretty.

265
00:08:58,840 --> 00:09:00,480
I remember you said
that you liked tulips.

266
00:09:00,480 --> 00:09:02,120
So I thought about it.

267
00:09:02,480 --> 00:09:03,160
Then I thought,

268
00:09:03,160 --> 00:09:04,640
let's get tulips.

269
00:09:05,080 --> 00:09:06,840
Then I have to keep this alive.

270
00:09:07,600 --> 00:09:09,280
You can pull off these leaves.

271
00:09:09,280 --> 00:09:10,760
So they won't take up the water.

272
00:09:10,760 --> 00:09:12,520
Just cut the stem
at an angle and put it in.

273
00:09:12,960 --> 00:09:14,300
It smells nice.

274
00:09:14,300 --> 00:09:14,640
Yeah.

275
00:09:14,640 --> 00:09:15,360
Just a little.

276
00:09:15,360 --> 00:09:16,520
Yeah, it smells pretty good

277
00:09:16,520 --> 00:09:17,600
So pretty.

278
00:09:17,600 --> 00:09:20,120
You look beautiful with this flower.

279
00:09:20,120 --> 00:09:21,160
(Praises)
Thank you.

280
00:09:21,160 --> 00:09:22,720
We should take a photo together here.

281
00:09:23,720 --> 00:09:24,280
Let's...

282
00:09:24,280 --> 00:09:24,680
Wait.

283
00:09:24,680 --> 00:09:25,680
Where's my camera?

284
00:09:25,680 --> 00:09:27,000
Let's take some photos.

285
00:09:27,000 --> 00:09:27,600
Sure.

286
00:09:27,600 --> 00:09:28,400
Wait a second.

287
00:09:30,660 --> 00:09:33,580
(Takes out camera)

288
00:09:34,120 --> 00:09:34,680
Come on, Si.

289
00:09:34,680 --> 00:09:36,120
Let me take a beautiful photo

290
00:09:37,080 --> 00:09:38,000
of you.

291
00:09:39,320 --> 00:09:41,200
Good. You look Korean.

292
00:09:42,120 --> 00:09:43,200
So pretty.

293
00:09:43,200 --> 00:09:44,160
Very retro.

294
